%I A401295 #7 Oct 27 2026 20:59:36
%S A401295 1,0,1,2,6,17,62,251,1251,7560,57177
%N A401295 Number of unlabeled n-element posets in which every element is completely join-irreducible.
%C A401295 Many of the small entries seem to consist of disjoint unions of trees.
%C A401295 Given any poset P, substitute all elements x with two elements x_0 and x_1, with the ordering x_i < y_j iff x < y. That is, replace all elements with size-2 antichains. Then, all elements are join-irreducible. This makes a structural characterization of this class somewhat elusive; it includes all posets given the proper substitutions.
%H A401295 Elisha Goldman, <a href="https://irreducible-posets.ponensmoder.chatgpt.site/?n=5&amp;k=5&amp;p=1">Join-irreducible counts in posets</a> (see main diagonal)
%H A401295 Brendan McKay, <a href="https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/data/digraphs.html">Catalogues of unlabeled posets</a>.
%e A401295 a(0) = 1 because the empty poset satisfies the condition vacuously.
%e A401295 a(1) = 0 because the unique element of the singleton poset is the join of the empty set.
%e A401295 a(3) = 2: the three-element antichain and the disjoint union of a two-element chain and a singleton.
%Y A401295 Diagonal of A400798.
%Y A401295 Cf. A000112 (all unlabeled posets).
%K A401295 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A401295 0,4
